<!--
  Deliberately empty, and load-bearing, for the same reason as Directory.Build.props beside it —
  and needed separately, which is the part that was missed.

  MSBuild walks up for Directory.Build.props and again, independently, for Directory.Build.targets.
  Shadowing the props alone left the second walk to reach the repository's own targets, which adds
  Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers to every project under it. So the fixtures were carrying
  this repository's public-API analyzer while their props file explained that whatever they need
  they declare themselves: RS0016 was in InvalidContract's build log, ten times.

  A fixture exists to imitate somebody else's project consuming us from nuget.org. Somebody else's
  project does not have our analyzers in it.
-->
<Project />
